hmetic-function-characterization","thm-dirichlet-character-orthogonality","thm-dirichlet-l-euler-product","thm-primes-residue-class-dirichlet-density"]},{"convention":"Natural/Dirichlet density of subsets of N uses (s-1)Σn∈A n^-s as s↓1, whereas prime-relative Dirichlet density uses the coefficient of log(1/(s-1)).","fixed_by":"def-natural-and-dirichlet-density","matters_for":["thm-natural-density-implies-dirichlet-density","thm-primes-residue-class-dirichlet-density","cex-dirichlet-density-does-not-mean-integer-natural-density"]},{"convention":"(a,b)_v=1 means ax²+by²=1 is soluble over Q_v; Q_∞ is R and Q_p is the p-adic completion.","fixed_by":"def-hilbert-symbol-over-a-rational-completion","matters_for":["lem-equivalent-definitions-of-the-hilbert-symbol","thm-odd-p-hilbert-symbol-formula","thm-two-adic-hilbert-symbol-formula","cor-ternary-isotropy-via-hilbert-symbol","thm-hilbert-reciprocity-over-the-rationals"]},{"convention":"A PCP match is a nonempty sequence of whole dominoes, with literal concatenation; modified PCP additionally requires its first domino to be tile 1.","fixed_by":"def-post-correspondence-problem","matters_for":["def-modified-post-correspondence-problem","lem-computation-history-domino-encoding","lem-modified-pcp-reduces-to-pcp","thm-cfg-intersection-emptiness-is-undecidable","thm-cfg-ambiguity-is-undecidable"]},{"convention":"Numberings are indexed by N including 0, and multi-input programs are unary programs receiving the stipulated recursive finite-sequence code.","fixed_by":"def-numbering-of-partial-computable-functions","matters_for":["def-universal-and-acceptable-numbering","def-parameter-specialization-function","thm-smn-parameter-theorem","thm-kleenes-second-recursion-theorem"]},{"convention":"CLIQUE and INDEPENDENT SET use witnesses of size at least k, while VERTEX COVER uses a witness of size at most k.","fixed_by":"def-clique-independent-set-and-vertex-cover-problems","matters_for":["thm-three-sat-reduces-to-clique","thm-clique-independent-set-and-vertex-cover-are-polynomially-interreducible","thm-three-sat-reduces-to-subset-sum","thm-vertex-cover-reduces-to-set-cover"]}],"load_bearing":[{"id":"thm-hasse-minkowski-over-the-rationals","statement":"Let q be a nondegenerate quadratic form over Q. Then q is isotropic over Q if and only if it is isotropic over R and over Q_p for every prime p.","used_by":["ex-hasse-minkowski-for-a-quaternary-form","cex-rational-isotropy-is-not-integral-representation"]},{"id":"thm-dirichlet-l-nonzero-at-one","statement":"If χ≠χ₀ is a Dirichlet character, then L(1,χ)≠0.","used_by":["thm-primes-residue-class-dirichlet-density","thm-mertens-primes-arithmetic-progressions"]},{"id":"lem-computation-history-domino-encoding","statement":"For every coded deterministic one-tape Turing machine M and input word w, one can effectively construct a modified-PCP instance P_M,w having a match iff M has an accepting computation history on w.","used_by":["thm-modified-pcp-is-undecidable","ex-modified-pcp-is-undecidable"]},{"id":"thm-smn-parameter-theorem","statement":"If (φ_e) is an acceptable numbering, then for every m,n∈N there exists a parameter-specialization function s_m^n.","used_by":["cor-effective-program-specialization","lem-self-reference-construction-from-smn","thm-recursion-theorem-with-parameters","ex-smn-parameter-theorem"]},{"id":"thm-three-sat-reduces-to-directed-hamiltonian-cycle","statement":"There is a polynomial-time many-one reduction from 3-SAT to directed Hamiltonian cycle.","used_by":["cor-hamiltonian-path-and-cycle-are-np-complete"]},{"id":"thm-three-sat-reduces-to-clique","statement":"There is a polynomial-time many-one reduction from 3-SAT to CLIQUE.","used_by":["cor-clique-is-np-complete","thm-three-sat-reduces-to-subset-sum","ex-clique-is-np-complete"]}],"published_dependencies":[{"id":"cor-cfl-membership-is-decidable","used_for":"CFL membership and the context-free-to-decidable inclusion.","opened":true},{"id":"cor-completely-multiplicative-dirichlet-